tive_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"as I worked on #6002 it became apparent that the connection pool no longer uses the \"reset agent\" under any circumstances outside of artificial ones in the test suite.  this is likely due to the rework of how transactions work starting with 0e53221eef50b3274841fbd1eb41e .\r\n\r\nideally, the pool reset should be skippable if the connection itself has actively emitted a ROLLBACK on the connection.  this could be achieved through the use of a new method on ConnectionFairy like _close_no_reset().   however, as the original purpose of the \"reset agent\", which was to use the already opened transaction for rollback, seems to no longer be a possible codepath, we should take out the whole \"reset agent\" thing altogether.   the test suite for #6002 added some assertions to validate that this is the case.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type"